('127.395.d.1.A',3,'A robotics engineer is most likely to:','["drive a delivery truck", "stock shelves", "design a new robotic system", "answer phones"]'::jsonb,2,'Engineers design systems.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.A',4,'A robotics technician most often:','["files taxes", "manages a restaurant", "writes laws", "installs, tests, and repairs robots"]'::jsonb,3,'Technicians support working systems.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.B',3,'Which industry uses robots to weld and assemble vehicles?','["Automotive manufacturing", "Barbering", "Bookkeeping", "Dairy farming"]'::jsonb,0,'Car plants rely on robots.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.B',4,'A professional who combines robots, sensors, and controllers into a working production cell is a:','["travel agent", "robot systems integrator", "lifeguard", "court reporter"]'::jsonb,1,'Integrators build complete cells.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.C',3,'Certifications in robotics show that a worker:','["owns a robot", "wrote a manual", "has proven skills in robot programming or safety", "avoided training"]'::jsonb,2,'Certifications verify skills.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.C',4,'A manufacturer such as FANUC offers training certificates for workers who:','["paint houses", "grow crops", "sell groceries", "program and maintain its robots"]'::jsonb,3,'Vendor training is job-specific.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.D',3,'Robot designers have an ethical duty to ensure that robots do not:','["endanger people nearby", "use batteries", "look modern", "cost money"]'::jsonb,0,'Safety comes first.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.D',4,'Ethics questions about automation include its effect on:','["ocean tides", "workers'' jobs", "moon phases", "paint colors"]'::jsonb,1,'Automation changes employment.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.E',3,'In a robotics club, welcoming students of all skill levels and backgrounds helps the team:','["avoid learning", "ignore ideas", "solve problems with more perspectives", "lose members"]'::jsonb,2,'Diverse views improve designs.','original'),
('127.395.d.1.E',4,'Respecting teammates'' cultural differences on a robotics project means:','["ignoring their input", "assigning work by stereotype", "excluding quiet members", "valuing each member''s contributions"]'::jsonb,3,'Respect is inclusive.','original'),
