('127.395.d.5.C',3,'In a robot with feedback, a sensor reports the arm''s position back to the:','["paint", "floor", "controller", "wheels"]'::jsonb,2,'Feedback closes the loop.','original'),
('127.395.d.5.C',4,'Feedback control lets a robot correct its:','["name", "weight", "color", "errors while moving"]'::jsonb,3,'Corrections use measured error.','original'),
('127.395.d.5.D',3,'A sensor that measures distance to an object using sound is an:','["ultrasonic sensor", "microphone", "strain gauge", "thermocouple"]'::jsonb,0,'Ultrasonic sensors time echoes.','original'),
('127.395.d.5.D',4,'Which sensor helps a line-following robot tell a dark line from a bright floor?','["Encoder", "Light or color sensor", "Gyroscope", "Thermistor"]'::jsonb,1,'Reflectance differs.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.A',3,'Newton''s second law states that force equals mass times:','["time", "velocity", "acceleration", "distance"]'::jsonb,2,'F = ma.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.A',4,'A heavier robot needs more force to speed up. This illustrates Newton''s:','["zeroth law", "third law", "first law", "second law"]'::jsonb,3,'Force relates to mass and acceleration.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.B',3,'When a small gear drives a larger gear, the output speed is:','["lower but torque is higher", "unchanged", "higher and torque is higher", "higher but torque is lower"]'::jsonb,0,'Speed trades for torque.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.B',4,'A 20-tooth driver gear meshed with a 60-tooth driven gear has a gear ratio of:','["1:3", "3:1", "6:1", "20:1"]'::jsonb,1,'60 / 20 = 3.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.C',3,'Which of these is one of the six simple machines?','["Battery", "Sensor", "Lever", "Transistor"]'::jsonb,2,'Lever, wheel and axle, pulley, inclined plane, wedge, screw.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.C',4,'A wheel and axle in a robot drivetrain is used to:','["store charge", "cool the motors", "detect light", "transmit rotation to move the robot"]'::jsonb,3,'It converts motor rotation into motion.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.D',3,'Reversing the polarity of the voltage across a DC motor makes it:','["spin in the opposite direction", "overheat", "spin faster", "stop forever"]'::jsonb,0,'Polarity sets direction.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.D',4,'Pulse width modulation controls the speed of a DC motor by changing the:','["motor color", "average voltage delivered", "shaft length", "wire gauge"]'::jsonb,1,'Duty cycle sets average power.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.E',3,'A hobby servo typically rotates its output shaft through about:','["3,600 degrees", "0 degrees", "180 degrees", "10 degrees"]'::jsonb,2,'Standard servos span about 180 degrees.','original'),
('127.395.d.6.E',4,'In a standard hobby servo, a 1.5 millisecond pulse usually commands the:','["power-off state", "full rotation loop", "maximum speed", "center position"]'::jsonb,3,'1.5 ms is neutral.','original'),
('127.395.d.7.A',3,'A longer robot arm that holds a load at its end creates more:','["torque at the base joint", "color", "voltage", "noise"]'::jsonb,0,'Torque = force x distance.','original'),
('127.395.d.7.A',4,'Using lightweight, rigid materials for arm links helps reduce the load on the:','["wall", "motors", "paint", "desk"]'::jsonb,1,'Less mass means less torque needed.','original'),
('127.395.d.7.B',3,'To lift a heavier payload with the same motor, increase the gear reduction, which raises:','["payload price", "motor color", "output torque", "input voltage"]'::jsonb,2,'Reduction multiplies torque.','original'),
('127.395.d.7.B',4,'A motor produces 2 newton-meters of torque and drives through a 5:1 reduction gearbox. The ideal output torque is:','["7 newton-meters", "0.4 newton-meters", "2 newton-meters", "10 newton-meters"]'::jsonb,3,'2 x 5 = 10.','original'),
('127.395.d.7.C',3,'The part at the end of a robot arm that grips or manipulates objects is the:','["end effector", "battery", "controller", "base"]'::jsonb,0,'Grippers are end effectors.','original'),
('127.395.d.7.C',4,'A gripper that uses a gear and rack to open and close converts rotary motion to:','["heat", "linear motion", "sound", "light"]'::jsonb,1,'Rack and pinion.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.A',3,'The design process begins by:','["recycling parts", "building the final robot", "identifying the problem or need", "selling the design"]'::jsonb,2,'Define the problem first.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.A',4,'After building a robot prototype, the design process calls for you to:','["ignore results", "ship it", "finish the report only", "test it against the requirements"]'::jsonb,3,'Testing follows building.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.B',3,'A competition rule limiting the robot to 18 inches is a:','["constraint", "sensor", "reward", "goal"]'::jsonb,0,'Rules limit designs.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.B',4,'Choosing a motor based on measured torque data, not opinion, is a:','["popularity vote", "fact-based decision", "guess", "coin flip"]'::jsonb,1,'Data supports choices.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.C',3,'Making changes after testing and then testing again is called:','["duplication", "deletion", "iteration", "repetition of errors"]'::jsonb,2,'Iteration improves designs.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.C',4,'A robot misses its target by the same amount every time. The team should:','["blame the floor", "stop testing", "ignore it", "adjust the design and retest"]'::jsonb,3,'Systematic error can be corrected.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.D',3,'A decision matrix scores design options against:','["weighted criteria", "team names", "colors only", "birthdays"]'::jsonb,0,'Matrices rank options.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.D',4,'Which strategy compares the pros and cons of each option before deciding?','["Random choice", "Trade-off analysis", "Coin tossing", "Skipping the choice"]'::jsonb,1,'Trade-offs weigh benefits and costs.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.E',3,'Quality control in robot production checks that each part meets:','["fashion trends", "nicknames", "specifications", "team slogans"]'::jsonb,2,'Specs define acceptable parts.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.E',4,'Inspecting gears with a gauge to catch out-of-tolerance parts is an example of:','["marketing", "shipping", "recycling", "quality control"]'::jsonb,3,'Inspection catches defects.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.F',3,'Customers judge a robot''s quality partly by its reliability and:','["ease of use", "shipping box color", "brand font", "company slogan"]'::jsonb,0,'Usability affects perceived quality.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.F',4,'A product that fails often will damage how customers perceive its:','["package", "quality and the company''s reputation", "color", "price tag"]'::jsonb,1,'Failures hurt trust.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.G',3,'In an engineering notebook for a robot project, you record design decisions and the:','["gossip", "weather", "reasons for them", "lunch"]'::jsonb,2,'Rationale is documented.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.G',4,'Notebook entries should be written in:','["random order", "pencil and erased", "code only", "ink with date and signature"]'::jsonb,3,'Permanent, dated entries.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.H',3,'A system schematic for a robot shows how the controller connects to the:','["motors and sensors", "windows", "furniture", "desks"]'::jsonb,0,'Schematics show connections.','original'),
('127.395.d.8.H',4,'Standard symbols on a robot wiring schematic let different engineers:','["hide connections", "read the diagram the same way", "avoid wiring", "change meanings"]'::jsonb,1,'Standards give shared meaning.','original'),
('127.395.d.9.A',3,'When using a hand saw on robot frame material, secure the workpiece with a:','["a friend''s foot", "a towel", "clamp or vise", "your hand"]'::jsonb,2,'Clamping prevents injury.','original'),
('127.395.d.9.A',4,'Safety glasses are required when using:','["only tape", "only paper", "only pencils", "cutting, drilling, or grinding tools"]'::jsonb,3,'Chips and sparks endanger eyes.','original'),
('127.395.d.9.B',3,'A digital caliper can measure a robot part''s width to:','["a hundredth of an inch or finer", "a foot only", "a mile", "a guess"]'::jsonb,0,'Calipers read fine increments.','original'),
('127.395.d.9.B',4,'Measuring a motor driver''s output with a multimeter helps verify the:','["paint thickness", "voltage supplied to the motor", "robot''s name", "room temperature"]'::jsonb,1,'Meters verify electrical outputs.','original'),
('127.395.d.9.C',3,'Robot simulation software lets a team test code:','["without a program", "after the competition", "before running it on the real robot", "only on paper"]'::jsonb,2,'Simulation reduces risk.','original'),
('127.395.d.9.C',4,'A simulation can help a team find path-planning errors without risking:','["a lunch break", "a sunny day", "a bus ride", "damage to the robot"]'::jsonb,3,'Errors occur virtually.','original'),
('127.395.d.10.A',3,'A prototype of a robot arm is built to:','["test the design before final production", "avoid testing", "sell immediately", "replace the design"]'::jsonb,0,'Prototypes reveal problems.','original'),
('127.395.d.10.A',4,'The first step in producing a prototype is usually to:','["ship it", "create drawings or models", "paint it", "retire it"]'::jsonb,1,'Plans precede building.','original'),
('127.395.d.10.B',3,'A 3D printer is useful in prototyping robot parts because it can:','["measure voltage", "weld steel", "quickly make custom shapes", "wire the controller"]'::jsonb,2,'Additive manufacturing is fast for custom parts.','original'),
('127.395.d.10.B',4,'Aluminum is often chosen for robot frames because it is strong and:','["very heavy", "magnetic", "a perfect insulator", "lightweight"]'::jsonb,3,'Strength-to-weight ratio.','original'),
('127.395.d.10.C',3,'When assembling a robot chassis, fasteners should be tightened until:','["snug without stripping threads", "they are loose", "they break", "they crack"]'::jsonb,0,'Over-tightening strips threads.','original'),
('127.395.d.10.C',4,'Wiring a robot neatly, with labels and strain relief, helps with:','["weight gain", "troubleshooting and reliability", "color", "noise"]'::jsonb,1,'Clean wiring is easier to maintain.','original'),
('127.395.d.10.D',3,'A robot must lift 2 kg. The team tests it with a 2 kg load to see if it meets the:','["rumor", "logo", "requirement", "mood"]'::jsonb,2,'Tests verify requirements.','original')
