('127.395.d.10.F',4,'A good presentation of a robot project uses photos, data, and a:','["guess", "long silence", "blank slide", "live demonstration"]'::jsonb,3,'Demos prove performance.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.A',3,'A robot wheel has a diameter of 4 inches. Using 3.14 for pi, how far does it travel in one full rotation?','["12.56 inches", "50.24 inches", "25.12 inches", "6.28 inches"]'::jsonb,0,'C = pi x d = 3.14 x 4.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.A',4,'A robot drives 10 feet in 4 seconds. Its average speed is:','["0.4 feet per second", "2.5 feet per second", "40 feet per second", "6 feet per second"]'::jsonb,1,'10 / 4 = 2.5.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.B',3,'A robot overshoots its target distance. Which step of a problem-solving model asks whether the fix is reasonable?','["Collecting parts", "Formulating a plan", "Evaluating the solution", "Analyzing the given information"]'::jsonb,2,'Evaluation checks reasonableness.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.B',4,'A technician first lists the robot''s measured speed and the course length. This is which step?','["Evaluating the process", "Justifying the answer", "Presenting results", "Analyzing given information"]'::jsonb,3,'Listing data is analysis.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.C',3,'To quickly check that a travel time of 3 seconds for 6 meters at 2 meters per second is reasonable, use:','["mental math", "a ruler", "a compass", "a thermometer"]'::jsonb,0,'6 / 2 = 3.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.C',4,'To plot encoder counts versus time and fit a trend line, an appropriate tool is:','["a tape measure", "a spreadsheet or graphing software", "a level", "a stopwatch alone"]'::jsonb,1,'Software handles data fitting.','original'),
