('127.396.d.1.F',4,'Because a motor''s output force and speed trade off at constant power, raising speed lowers:','["voltage rating", "weight", "color", "torque"]'::jsonb,3,'P = torque x speed.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.G',3,'To justify that a robot reached 90 degrees, a student should present the measurement and the:','["calculation or evidence", "slogan", "guess", "opinion"]'::jsonb,0,'Evidence supports claims.','original'),
('127.396.d.1.G',4,'Precise language in a robotics report means using correct units and terms such as:','["fast and slow", "torque and velocity", "stuff and things", "big and small"]'::jsonb,1,'Technical terms are exact.','original'),
('127.396.d.2.A',3,'A well-functioning robotics team has clear roles and:','["no deadlines", "secret plans", "open communication", "one member only"]'::jsonb,2,'Teams need clarity and talk.','original'),
('127.396.d.2.A',4,'Team members who each know their role on a competition robot reduce:','["progress", "quality", "safety", "confusion and duplicated work"]'::jsonb,3,'Roles prevent overlap.','original'),
('127.396.d.2.B',3,'When the robot''s code and hardware disagree, the programmers and builders should:','["troubleshoot together", "quit", "work separately", "blame each other"]'::jsonb,0,'Joint troubleshooting finds causes.','original'),
('127.396.d.2.B',4,'Sharing test data with all team members helps them to:','["hide failures", "make informed decisions together", "duplicate effort", "avoid the problem"]'::jsonb,1,'Shared data aligns decisions.','original'),
('127.396.d.2.C',3,'On a project, following the project lead''s decisions even when you disagree is part of:','["skipping tasks", "going alone", "working as a team", "breaking rules"]'::jsonb,2,'Teams need direction.','original'),
('127.396.d.2.C',4,'During a robot test, the safety officer tells everyone to stand back. You should:','["finish your task first", "ignore it", "argue", "comply immediately"]'::jsonb,3,'Safety directions are followed at once.','original'),
